pr_body:
Closes https://github.com/elastic/elasticsearch/issues/105005

The motivation for this PR is to conditionally expose the `dimensions` field already stored in the openai service settings. The openai API will only accept the `dimensions` field if the `model` is one of the `text-embedding-3-*` models.

For documentation details: https://platform.openai.com/docs/api-reference/embeddings/create
https://platform.openai.com/docs/models/embeddings

This was complicated for a couple reasons. Normally we could just add the new field in the openai service settings. Unfortunately a field called `dimensions` already exists to help with defining the `dense_vector` mapping. We set this field specifically for 3rd party services like openai during the creation process of the inference endpoint for text embeddings. We make a request and note the array size in the response to determine the dimensions. So for all 3rd party text embedding inference endpoint configurations, the `dimensions` field should be set automatically.

The problem is we only want to send this `dimensions` field if the _**user**_ has set the field while creating the inference endpoint.

I can think of a couple solutions:

1. Create a new field like `user_dimensions` which if set we'll send on with the request to openai
When an inference endpoint is created and the model is returned we'd see something like this:

```
{
    "model_id": "openai",
    "task_type": "text_embedding",
    "service": "cohere",
    "service_settings": {
        "similarity": "dot_product",
        "dimensions": 123, <--- this would be set automatically by us (or maybe we could not set it if user_dimensions` is set)
        "user_dimensions": 123,
        "model": "some model"
    },
    "task_settings": {
    }
}
```
2. Create a hidden boolean field that gets set if the user did include the `dimensions` field in their original inference endpoint creation request

When the an inference endpoint is created and the model is returned we wouldn't see this new hidden field and everything would look the same as before.

```
{
    "model_id": "openai",
    "task_type": "text_embedding",
    "service": "cohere",
    "service_settings": {
        "similarity": "dot_product",
        "dimensions": 123,
        "model": "some model"
    },
    "task_settings": {
    }
}
```

I went with the second because I figured that'd be less confusing for users and I figured we'd likely have some internal fields that we'll likely need to hide in the future.


_Hidden fields_ are still stored along side the other fields within the index in elasticsearch but they won't be included in any responses that would return a model.

Most of the changes are to support hidden fields. All existing openai text embedding inference endpoints will have the new hidden field `dimensionsSetByUser` defaulted to `false`. If the user had set them for some reason and they are expecting the dimensions to be passed through (they weren't anyway previous to this PR) they'll just need to delete their inference endpoint and recreate it.

## Testing

### Setting dimensions with an incompatible model
```
PUT _inference/text_embedding/openai
{
    "service": "openai",
    "service_settings": {
        "api_key": "${api_key}",
        "organization_id": "${org}",
        "max_input_tokens": 512,
        "dimensions": 5
    },
    "task_settings": {
      "model_id": "text-embedding-ada-002"
    }
}
```

Response
```
{
  "error": {
    "root_cause": [
      {
        "type": "status_exception",
        "reason": "Received an unsuccessful status code for request from inference entity id [openai] status [400]. Error message: [This model does not support specifying dimensions.]"
      }
    ],
    "type": "status_exception",
    "reason": "Received an unsuccessful status code for request from inference entity id [openai] status [400]. Error message: [This model does not support specifying dimensions.]"
  },
  "status": 400
}
```

### Setting dimensions with a compatible model

```
PUT _inference/text_embedding/openai
{
    "service": "openai",
    "service_settings": {
        "api_key": "${api_key}",
        "organization_id": "${org}",
        "max_input_tokens": 512,
        "dimensions": 5
    },
    "task_settings": {
      "model_id": "text-embedding-3-small"
    }
}
```

Response
```
{
  "model_id": "openai",
  "task_type": "text_embedding",
  "service": "openai",
  "service_settings": {
    "organization_id": "org",
    "similarity": "dot_product",
    "dimensions": 5,
    "max_input_tokens": 512
  },
  "task_settings": {
    "model_id": "text-embedding-3-small"
  }
}

```

Inference request
```
POST _inference/text_embedding/openai
{
  "input": ["hello"],
  "task_settings": {
  }
}
```

Response
```
{
  "text_embedding": [
    {
      "embedding": [
        0.18924388,
        -0.6276148,
        0.06360514,
        0.74572676,
        0.100659885
      ]
    }
  ]
}
```

